A||||11||TRiAD||"Plastic" cars?!||||6||
Z||000000||TRiAD||12-07-2001||07:48 PM||||Hehe...Some of you may enjoy this...<P>I was talking with some friends, and some of <I>their</I> friends, and one of them hears us talking about the Fiero. <P>He starts spouting how <I>real</I> cars aren't plastic, and how he'd <I>hate</I> to get in a wreck in one...<P>I try telling him about the excellent crash rating, and the very advanced (IMHO) chassis under our cars, and he's as stubborn as ever. "Real cars aren't plastic!"<P>I explain the body panels are the only unusual plastic part of the car (trying not to make a Saturn reference), and yet, he persists with his ignorance...<P>So, after hearing him ring his own bell till the clanger fell off; toot his own horn till the bell fell off; pat his own back at the expense of his arm; I finally ask; "So, there, Mr. Smartypants; what DO you consider a "real" car?"<P>His answer?<P>Are you ready for it?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Are you sitting down?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P><B><FONT COLOR="red">A CORVETTE!</B></FONT><P>I about laughed my butt off! EVERYONE with us (even the ones who give me crap) were laughing at him! <P>What a moron!<P><I>Disclaimer; Corvettes are indeed very nice cars, they could be made a bit better, but that's hardly the point...In case you missed it; he was ragging on plastic cars...The Corvette has plastic body panels, just like Fieros...</I><BR><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://communities.msn.com/_Secure/0RAAAAN8VWdTblRDE93zkbJ*AbWuOFSwE0rtNS2h23KCe3aGgj1O!JDqud!IoFt1NPvdq6rh9ef*226xJh!nSf*vv2Id5gL8WoDCkDX*tCeM/1985-Signature-2.gif">    <BR><B><I><FONT COLOR="blue">Project MR1 ~ triadtuning@hotmail.com</B> ~ Photoshop rendition of planned modifications</I></FONT>||||reg||6
