Z||000006||Oreif||12-08-2001||01:39 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 88-DOHC:<BR><B>haha, pretty funny, especially since I don't think there has ever been a an entire metal body corvette ever made. Either all figerglass or what they have now (fiberglass/plastic mixure much like Fiero). Personally I think I would rather be in a Fiero then a vette in a crash.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>There was a metal Corvette! The first year 1953 the body was metal. 1954 the body was changed to Fiberglass. I don't know how many 53's were made but I think it was a very small number. <BR>Just one of those little things you read about and it ends up being some trvia type of answer years later.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>||||reg||1
Z||000007||88-DOHC||12-08-2001||02:09 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Oreif:<BR><B> There was a metal Corvette! The first year 1953 the body was metal. 1954 the body was changed to Fiberglass. I don't know how many 53's were made but I think it was a very small number. <BR>Just one of those little things you read about and it ends up being some trvia type of answer years later.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>hehe, well now I know. Having nothing more then general corvette knowledge, I only knew they had used fiberglass for the body. Didn't think they had actually made a metal body, but I suppose it kind of makes sense that the first year would have been.  In any case, I will file that little piece of trivia in the same place I put all little pieces of trivia. In my brain where I will most likely promptly forget it.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
