Z||000009||rogergarrison||12-08-2001||11:59 AM||||Well, I have all 3, or 4 if you count kit.<P>1. Fiero<BR>2. the Ferrari kit on it<BR>3. Corvette<BR>4. Lumina mini van work/tow<P>There all plastic in one form or another. Being a body shop owner, I hate fixing rust. The van gets about 50 miles a month avg, so it would be a rust bucket by now.||||reg||1
Z||000010||Songman||12-08-2001||06:27 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Oreif:<BR><B> There was a metal Corvette! The first year 1953 the body was metal. 1954 the body was changed to Fiberglass. I don't know how many 53's were made but I think it was a very small number. <BR>Just one of those little things you read about and it ends up being some trvia type of answer years later.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Hate to disagree with you, Oreif.. but the 1953 Corvette was also made of fiberglass. There were 300 produced.<P>Check this link for verification. <A HREF="http://www.netvettes.com/1953.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.netvettes.com/1953.html</A> <P>||||reg||1
Z||000011||Bruce||12-08-2001||08:31 PM||||Yesterday I didn't set the e-brake correctly, and my Fiero rolled downhill about 15yds., hit a big rock and moved it back about 4'. The left bumper, near the exhaust pipes, was scraped and indented. When I returned in about half an hour, the bump had had "corrected itself," and only a minor scrape remains. Gotta love that Enduraflex!<BR>bb||||reg||1
